    "policy_pages": [
      {
        "id": "32",
        "account_id": "00d6bbb6-4ae9-450f-a6dd-81267bdd4ee1",
        "policy_id": "8782e617-c7e4-4ba5-a790-201d90924d22",
        "page_number": 1,
        "text": "MERIDIAN HARBOUR ASSURANCE\nENDORSEMENT\nEndorsement no.\tPolicy number\tPolicy owner\nME-26-0412\tMHA-HC-2025-0748213\tSimon Alastair Hartwell\nPlan\tDate of issue\tEffective date of this endorsement\nSafeStay Family Hospital Cash & Personal Accident Plan\t18 June 2026\t01 July 2026\nAt the request of the Policy Owner and in consideration of the revised premium, it is hereby declared and agreed that,\nwith effect from 01 July 2026, the Schedule of Benefits of the above Policy is amended as follows:\nItem\tBenefit\tCategory\tExisting\tRevised\nB\tHospital daily allowance (per day of confinement)\tChild (each)\tS$80 per day\tS$110 per day\nThe revised amount applies to days of Confinement falling on or after the effective date. Days of Confinement before 01\nJuly 2026 remain payable at the Existing amount.\nThe maximum of 60 days per policy year, the Adult amounts and all other terms, conditions and exclusions of the Policy\nremain unchanged.\nThis Endorsement forms part of and must be attached to Policy MHA-HC-2025-0748213.\nFor and on behalf of Meridian Harbour Assurance Pte. Ltd.\n____________________________\nAuthorised Signatory, Policy Services\nMeridian Harbour Assurance Pte. Ltd. (fictional) | Endorsement ME-26-0412 to Policy MHA-HC-2025-0748213\tPage 1 of 1",
        "extraction_method": "native"
      },
      {
        "id": "33",
        "account_id": "00d6bbb6-4ae9-450f-a6dd-81267bdd4ee1",
        "policy_id": "febfa399-8dad-46b7-965a-9c424360f0e6",
        "page_number": 1,
        "text": "MERIDIAN HARBOUR ASSURANCE\nSafeStay Family Hospital Cash & Personal Accident Plan — Policy Schedule\nPolicy number\tPolicy owner\tPeriod of cover\nMHA-HC-2025-0748213\tSimon Alastair Hartwell\t01 February 2026 to 31 January 2027 (both dates inclusive)\nPlan type: Family (2 Adults + 2 Children). Currency: Singapore Dollars (S$). Cover basis: Accident only — see Clause\n3.1.\nInsured Persons\nNo.\tName of Insured Person\tCategory\tDate of birth\tRelationship to owner\n1\tSimon Alastair Hartwell\tAdult\t17/03/1984\tSelf\n2\tLeonie Brigitte Hartwell\tAdult\t02/11/1986\tSpouse\n3\tFelix Oran Hartwell\tChild\t21/06/2017\tSon\n4\tIsla Maren Hartwell\tChild\t09/01/2020\tDaughter\nSchedule of Benefits\nItem\tBenefit\tAdult (each)\tChild (each)\nA\tAccidental death or permanent total disablement (lump sum)\tS$150,000\tS$40,000\nB\tHospital daily allowance (per day of confinement, max 60 days per policy year) — see Clause 4.2\tS$120 per day\tS$80 per day\nC\tIntensive care unit allowance (payable in addition to Item B, max 10 days per policy year)\tS$250 per day\tS$180 per day\nD\tFractured bones (per Accident) — Simple (closed) fracture\tS$1,000\tS$600\nE\tFractured bones (per Accident) — Compound (open) fracture\tS$2,500\tS$1,500\nF\tMedical expenses due to Accident (per Accident, reimbursement)\tup to S$3,000\tup to S$2,000\nG\tMobility aids & home modification (once per policy year)\tup to S$1,500\tup to S$1,000\nItems D and E: the type of fracture must be certified in writing by a registered medical practitioner and confirmed by X-ray. Only one of Item D or\nItem E is payable for the same bone in the same Accident. See Clause 4.4.\nThis Schedule must be read together with the Policy Wording on page 2. Issued in Singapore on 24 January 2026.\nMeridian Harbour Assurance Pte. Ltd. (fictional) | Co. Reg. No. 201899999Z | SafeStay Family Plan Policy Schedule | MHA-HC-2025-0748213 Page 1 of 2",
        "extraction_method": "native"
      },
      {
        "id": "34",
        "account_id": "00d6bbb6-4ae9-450f-a6dd-81267bdd4ee1",
        "policy_id": "febfa399-8dad-46b7-965a-9c424360f0e6",
        "page_number": 2,
        "text": "Policy Wording (extract)\n1. Definitions\n1.1 Accident means a sudden, unforeseen and involuntary event caused by external, violent and visible means,\noccurring during the Period of Cover.\n1.2 Confinement means admission as a registered in-patient in a licensed hospital in Singapore or overseas, on the\nwritten advice of a registered medical practitioner.\n2. Who is covered\n2.1 The Insured Persons named in the Schedule. A Child is covered from 30 days of age until the policy anniversary\nfollowing his or her 18th birthday.\n3. Scope of cover\n3.1 Accident-only cover. All benefits in this Policy, including Items B and C, are payable only where the Confinement or\nloss results solely and directly from an Accident and begins within 90 days of that Accident. Confinement due to illness or\ndisease is not covered.\n4. Benefit conditions\n4.1 Item B is payable for each day of Confinement up to the maximum number of days shown in the Schedule for each\nInsured Person in each policy year.\n4.2 How days of confinement are counted. Days are counted from the date and time of admission to the date and time\nof discharge shown on the hospital record. Each complete period of 24 consecutive hours counts as one day. Any\nremaining period of 12 hours or more counts as one further day; any remaining period of less than 12 hours is\ndisregarded. A Confinement of less than 12 hours in total is not payable. Days are not counted by calendar date or by the\nnumber of nights.\n4.3 Item C is payable only for the hours spent in an intensive care unit, counted in the same way as Clause 4.2.\n4.4 For Items D and E, a Compound fracture means a fracture in which the broken bone breaks through the skin. All\nother fractures are Simple fractures. Hairline fractures and stress fractures are treated as Simple fractures.\n5. Exclusions\nWe will not pay any benefit for any loss, Confinement or expense directly or indirectly caused by or arising from:\n5.1 intentional self-injury, suicide or attempted suicide, while sane or insane;\n5.2 participation in professional sports, motor racing, scuba diving below 30 metres, sky-diving or mountaineering\nrequiring ropes or guides;\n5.3 pregnancy, childbirth or miscarriage;\n5.4 war, invasion, act of foreign enemy, civil war, rebellion, or nuclear, chemical or biological contamination;\n5.5 the Insured Person being under the influence of alcohol above the legal driving limit or of drugs not prescribed by a\nmedical practitioner.\n6. Claims\n6.1 Written notice of a claim must be given within 30 days of the Accident. Claims must be supported by the hospital\ndischarge summary showing date and time of admission and discharge, original bills, and any medical certification\nrequired by this Policy.\n6.2 Claims may be submitted at meridianharbour.example/claims or by post to Claims Department, 8 Harbourfront Walk\n#11-02, Singapore 098999.\nMeridian Harbour Assurance Pte. Ltd. (fictional) | Co. Reg. No. 201899999Z | SafeStay Family Plan Policy Schedule | MHA-HC-2025-0748213 Page 2 of 2",
        "extraction_method": "native"
      }
